    <!-- ================= PART 2: INTERNATIONAL SHIPPING (2026 POLICY) ================= -->
    <div id="international-shipping" style="margin-bottom: 5rem;">
      <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        <span style="font-size: 2.2rem;">✈️</span>
        <h2 class="ga-title" style="font-size: 2.4rem; font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif, 'Playfair Display', serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green, #1a332c); margin: 0;">
          Part 2: International Shipping, Customs &amp; Refund Policy (2026 Edition)
        </h2>
      </div>

      <!-- Introductory Transparency Statement -->
      <div class="ga-callout-box" style="margin-top: 1.5rem; background: #faf8f5; border-color: rgba(26, 51, 44, 0.2);">
        <h3 class="ga-callout-title" style="font-size: 1.75rem;">
          <span>📋</span> Purpose &amp; Regulatory Transparency
        </h3>
        <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300; margin: 0;">
          This policy explains how Ghar Aangan currently handles international orders for food products, particularly Pure A2 Bilona Cow Ghee. It is designed to make international ordering, shipping, customs, delivery, additional charges, and refunds as transparent as possible.
          <br><br>
          <em>Please Note: This is an operating customer-information policy, not formal legal advice. International food-import, customs, dairy, courier, and tax rules are subject to change. Destination authorities make the final decision regarding import clearance. A courier’s ability to quote or accept a parcel does not itself establish that the food is legally admissible for commercial import or sale.</em>
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Current Five-Country Rationale & Status -->
      <div style="margin-top: 3.5rem;">
        <h3 class="ga-title" style="font-size: 2.1rem; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green);">
          5. Active International Markets &amp; Country Status
        </h3>
        <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.5rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          International shipping is currently available to <strong>selected countries</strong>. These five target markets were selected due to strong Indian / South Asian diaspora demand, established international food-import channels, and India's existing dairy export activity (APEDA 2025–26 data lists the UAE, Saudi Arabia, and the USA among India's major dairy export destinations):
        </p>

        <!-- Desktop Country Table -->
        <div class="ga-desktop-country-table">
          <div class="ga-shipping-table-wrap">
            <table class="ga-shipping-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Country</th>
                  <th>Status</th>
                  <th>Key Regulatory &amp; Import Requirements</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇺🇸 United States (USA)</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-active">Active</span></td>
                  <td>FDA food requirements, facility registration, Prior Notice, compliant labelling, commercial invoice, accurate HS codes. U.S. de minimis rules changed on 29 August 2025; imports may be subject to duties/taxes regardless of shipment value.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇦🇪 United Arab Emirates (UAE)</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-active">Active</span></td>
                  <td>Dubai Municipality food-item and label assessment; clearance routes confirmed before dispatch; local importer requirements may apply.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇦🇺 Australia</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-active">Active</span></td>
                  <td>DAFF / BICON biosecurity, food standards, and dairy-specific import conditions. Australia dairy risk-management measures (Stage 2 beginning 1 September 2026); health certification verified prior to dispatch.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇸🇦 Saudi Arabia</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-active">Active</span></td>
                  <td>SFDA importer/product registration, certificate of origin, commercial invoice, bill of lading, and sanitary/health clearance documentation.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇸🇬 Singapore</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-active">Active</span></td>
                  <td>Singapore Food Agency (SFA) importer licensing, import permit, compliant labelling, and product-specific dairy health requirements.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇬🇧 United Kingdom (UK)</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-inactive">Not Active for Ghee</span></td>
                  <td>Current UK government guidance indicates dairy products originating in India are not imported because India does not have an approved veterinary residue plan for dairy under UK legislation; such products are considered non-compliant and can be detained. Ghar Aangan does not accept direct-to-consumer ghee orders to the UK.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong>🇨🇦 Canada</strong></td>
                  <td><span class="ga-badge-inactive">Not Active for Ghee</span></td>
                  <td>Canada is not currently activated for Ghar Aangan ghee pending product-specific Canadian / CFIA clearance.</td>
                </tr>
