        <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">• After Courier Booking or Dispatch</h4>
          <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300;">
            Once booked, picked up, or dispatched, courier freight, export documentation, and third-party fees are generally non-refundable. A customer changing their mind after dispatch is therefore not automatically entitled to a full refund. If a parcel recall is operationally possible, recoverable amounts are calculated after deducting courier freight, return freight, and administrative costs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">• Customs Rejection or Return</h4>
          <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300;">
            If a shipment is rejected because Ghar Aangan failed to provide a required export document or due to a Ghar Aangan-controlled compliance failure, the case will be reviewed for an appropriate refund or replacement after recovery of the shipment where possible.
            <br><br>
            If rejection or return occurs because destination regulations prohibit the product, the customer/importer cannot complete clearance, the recipient refuses required duties or charges, the address is invalid, or customer information is omitted, any refund will be reduced by non-refundable shipping, return carriage, customs, storage, and demurrage costs.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">• Damage in Transit</h4>
          <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300;">
            If an international parcel arrives damaged, contact Ghar Aangan promptly with unboxing photos/videos of the outer carton, shipping label, and damaged product. Retain all packaging until the courier claim is resolved. Ghar Aangan will investigate and process an applicable replacement or refund.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">• Lost Shipments</h4>
          <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300;">
            For an apparently lost international shipment, Ghar Aangan will initiate a carrier/insurance tracer. The customer remedy depends on the investigation outcome, declared value, recoverability, and applicable law. A temporary tracking scan delay is not automatically treated as final loss.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-bottom: 2rem;">
          <h4 style="font-family: var(--ga-font-family-serif); color: var(--ga-forest-green); font-size: 1.75rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem;">• Food Quality &amp; Taste Preference</h4>
          <p class="ga-body" style="font-size: 1.45rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ga-dark-text); font-weight: 300;">
            Due to strict international food hygiene regulations, opened or consumed ghee is not eligible for preference-based returns simply because a customer dislikes subjective taste, aroma, or granular texture. Genuine quality or safety defects must be reported promptly with supporting evidence.
